<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fontaine-lès-Dijon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fontaine-lès-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dijon">Dijon</a> is a small town just north of Dijon in the Côte-d'Or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>. It is the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernard-of-clairvaux">Bernard of Clairvaux</a>, born there in 1090 in the castle of his father, the knight Tescelin, and the site of his family home has long been a place of pilgrimage in his honour.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fontaine-les-dijon.jpg" alt="Fontaine-lès-Dijon" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ville de Fontaine-lès-Dijon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:H%C3%B4tel_de_Ville_de_Fontaine-l%C3%A8s-Dijon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
